One change to your research workflow

I wouldn't pull 2010–2014 and 2018–2022 and immediately label them "pre" and "post."

Instead, first pull the complete available series, including the transition years.

For NAEP, your raw data might look something like:

2011 → 2013 → 2015 → 2017 → 2019 → 2022

depending on the specific grade/subject assessment.

Then you decide analytically how to classify the periods.

That's actually much better for your paper because you'll be able to visualize the trends before making the treatment definition.

