And I would not pull the data manually one state at a time. Since you've already been working with the NAEP API, this is a perfect opportunity to build a reproducible Python acquisition script that systematically queries the state × year × grade × subject × subgroup combinations and saves the raw responses. That becomes part of the research artifact for your R1 applications.
